Tint the icons from the theme: upstream is dark only, and its icons are vector drawables
filled white with no tint, which the places that show them do not tint either (the toolbar's
settings action, the alarm's ringtone, vibrate and delete icons, the alarm volume setting,
the alarm screen's alarm button and the analog clock). In the light theme they showed white
on a light background. They take the theme's control colour (the analog clock and the alarm
button its on-surface colour) as their default tint, which a place that tints them still
replaces. The expand caret and the timer's close button stay white: they sit on a grey disc.
On the alarm screen the dismiss button's circle takes the on-surface colour, so that its
icon, which takes the window's colour, shows on it, and the snooze icon takes the colour that
reads on the snooze circle. The screensaver draws on black in both themes, so it takes the
dark theme's colours.

